# The ruling on Fblthp: a card that normally has plot may be plotted from the top for its own plot cost or for Fblthp's, its mana
# cost. The Blacksnag Buzzard on top has Plot {1}{B} and costs {2}{B}: with Mox Jet and a Swamp only {B}{B} is there, so the
# mana cost is refused (the first line, which is told by being short of mana) and its own plot cost is paid, exactly, leaving
# the pool empty; the Buzzard is plotted. Turn one ends with the Fblthp on the table.

